$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl
2-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinamido)acetate (INT-A): HATU (0.36 g, 0.96
mmol) and DIPEA (0.25 mL, 1.4 mmol) were added to a solution of
4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic acid (0.27 g, 0.80 mmol) in DMF (2 mL). After
10 min, methyl 2-aminoacetate HCl salt (0.1 g, 0.80 mmol) was added. The
reaction mixture was stirred at room temperature overnight. The mixture
was diluted with EtOAc, washed with brine, concentrated, and purified by
silica gel column chromatography (0-100% EtOAc in hexanes). (S)-Methyl
2-(4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinamido)-4-(methylthio)butanoate: The title
compound was synthesized similarly to INT-A using (S)-methyl
2-amino-4-(methylthio)butanoate HCl salt (190 mg, 0.95 mmol) and
4,5-bis(benzyloxy)picolinic acid (319 mg, 0.95 mmol). The reaction
mixture was diluted with EtOAc and washed with brine. The organic phase
was concentrated, and purified by silica gel column chromatography (0-50%
EtOAc in hexanes). The product as a clear oil (340 mg, 74%). 1H NMR (300
MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ ppm 8.74-8.94 (m, 1 H) 8.29 (s, 1 H) 7.71 (s, 1 H)
7.30-7.53 (m, 10 H) 5.33 (m, 4 H) 4.63 (m, 1 H) 3.64 (s, 3 H) 2.38-2.49
(m, 2 H) 2.05-2.21 (m, 2 H) 2.03 (s, 3 H). ESI-MS m/z: 481.1 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Efficacious Pseudomonas aeruginosa-Targeted
Siderophore-Conjugated Monocarbams by Application of a Semi-mechanistic
Pharmacokinetic/Pharmacodynamic Model
